            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5",
            "treatment.6"
          ],
          "text": "On admission he had a temperature of 37.6, RR 58, mild-moderate subcostal recession, widespread fine creps and wheeze, and sats of 90% on room air. NPA confirmed RSV positivity. He was managed with supplemental oxygen to maintain sats ≥90% and nasogastric feeds (with IV fluids as a contingency). No antibiotics were given given the viral aetiology, and salbutamol was not used as it is not indicated in bronchiolitis. By Day 2 his sats had improved to 93–95% on room air, RR had settled to 44, recession was mild only, oral feeding had improved to ~75%, wet nappies had returned, and both supplemental oxygen and the nasogastric tube were removed prior to discharge.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
